the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the calculation date is *a date*; scenario element.
    the minimum employment hours per week is *a number*.
    the employment or earnings exemption of *a person* applies.
    *a person* is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements; scenario element.
    the employed hours per week of *a person* is *a value*; scenario element.
    the weekly earnings of *a person* is *an amount*; scenario element.
    the minimum hourly rate under fair labor standards act of *a person* is *a rate*; scenario element.

the knowledge base us_statutes_7_2015_d_2_e includes:


% 7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(E) — us:statutes/7/2015/d/2/E
the text of "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(E)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/d/2/E.yaml".

the minimum employment hours per week is 30 if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D.

rule employment_or_earnings_exemption_applies_1 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(E)":
the employment or earnings exemption of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements
        and the employed hours per week of the person is a value V
        and the minimum employment hours per week is a number N
        and V >= N.

rule employment_or_earnings_exemption_applies_2 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2015(d)(2)(E)":
the employment or earnings exemption of a person applies if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the person is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements
        and the weekly earnings of the person is an amount N
        and the minimum hourly rate under fair labor standards act of the person is a rate R
        and the minimum employment hours per week is a number M
        and N >= R * M.

scenario employed_minimum_thirty_hours_per_week_exemption_applies is, as stated in "sources/us/statutes/7/2015/d/2/E.test.yaml" at case 1:
    person_1 is a person.
    the calculation date is 2026-01-01.
    the employed hours per week of person_1 is 30.
    the minimum hourly rate under fair labor standards act of person_1 is 8.
    person_1 is person otherwise required to comply with paragraph 1 requirements.
    the weekly earnings of person_1 is 0.
    q_employment_or_earnings_exemption_applies expects answers ["the employment or earnings exemption of person_1 applies"].

